 "description": "First-order RC low-pass or high-pass cutoff frequency: fc = 1/(2*pi*R*C), tau = R*C. LP and HP share the cutoff formula (response shape differs).\n\nArgs: type ('lowpass'|'highpass'), and exactly two of { r_ohm, c_farad, fc_hz } -> solves the third.\nReturns (structured): { fc_hz, r_ohm, c_farad, tau_s }.\nExample: R=10k, C=1uF -> fc 15.92 Hz. Common for ADC anti-aliasing / debounce. Snap the computed part with embedcalc_eseries_nearest.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "c_farad": {
    "description": "Capacitor in farads (100nF = 100e-9)",
    "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
    "type": "number"
   },
   "fc_hz": {
    "description": "Cutoff frequency in Hz",
    "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
    "type": "number"
   },
   "r_ohm": {
    "description": "Resistor in ohms",
    "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
    "type": "number"
   },
   "type": {
    "description": "Filter response type",
    "enum": [
     "lowpass",
     "highpass"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "type"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
 "name": "embedcalc_rc_filter",
